11:["$","p","i) It consists of 2 different essays :- issue task, argument task.",{"children":"i) It consists of 2 different essays :- issue task, argument task."}]
12:["$","p","ii) In issue task you would need to construct your own argument.",{"children":"ii) In issue task you would need to construct your own argument."}]
13:["$","p","iii) In argument task you would need to evaluate someone else’s argument.",{"children":"iii) In argument task you would need to evaluate someone else’s argument."}]
14:["$","p","iv) You will use a basic word processor developed by ETS to type your essay responses. (only insert text, delete text, cut-and-paste and undo the previous action)",{"children":"iv) You will use a basic word processor developed by ETS to type your essay responses. (only insert text, delete text, cut-and-paste and undo the previous action)"}]
15:["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Quantitative Reasoning:-",{"children":"Quantitative Reasoning:-"}],["$","li","Analytical Writing :-",{"children":"Analytical Writing :-"}]]}]
16:["$","section","WHAT IS GMAT EXAM ?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"WHAT IS GMAT EXAM ?"}],[["$","p","The full form of (GMAT) is graduate management admission test. It assess our analytical, verbal and writing skills and problem solving abilities. It is a multiple choice computer based standardized test. It is the top most exam taken to get into your preferred business school.",{"children":"The full form of (GMAT) is graduate management admission test. It assess our analytical, verbal and writing skills and problem solving abilities. It is a multiple choice computer based standardized test. It is the top most exam taken to get into your preferred business school."}],["$","p","This test is for people who are applying for management/business programs (MBA etc.)",{"children":"This test is for people who are applying for management/business programs (MBA etc.)"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
17:["$","section","GMAT exam pattern :-",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"GMAT exam pattern :-"}],[["$","p","i) Quantitative , ii) verbal iii) integrated reasoning and iv) analytical writing assessment.",{"children":"i) Quantitative , ii) verbal iii) integrated reasoning and iv) analytical writing assessment."}],["$","p","GMAT Exam fees :-",{"children":"GMAT Exam fees :-"}],["$","p","US $275 (INR 22,456.91)",{"children":"US $275 (INR 22,456.91)"}],["$","p","Sections of GMAT:-",{"children":"Sections of GMAT:-"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Quantitative Reasoning:-",{"children":"Quantitative Reasoning:-"}]]}]]}]
18:["$","section","i) In this section you would have 31 questions",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"i) In this section you would have 31 questions"}],[["$","p","ii) It consists of 2 problem types:- data sufficiency, problem solving.",{"children":"ii) It consists of 2 problem types:- data sufficiency, problem solving."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
19:["$","section","iv) 17-18(problem solving questions)",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"iv) 17-18(problem solving questions)"}],[["$","p","v) This section will test your mathematic knowledge and reasoning skills.",{"children":"v) This section will test your mathematic knowledge and reasoning skills."}],["$","p","i) In this section you would have 36 questions.",{"children":"i) In this section you would have 36 questions."}],["$","p","ii) It consists of 3 problem types:- critical reasoning, sentence correction, reading comprehension.",{"children":"ii) It consists of 3 problem types:- critical reasoning, sentence correction, reading comprehension."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Verbal Reasoning :-",{"children":"Verbal Reasoning :-"}]]}]]}]
1a:["$","section","iii) It will test your command of standard written english",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"iii) It will test your command of standard written english"}],[["$","p","iv) To check your ability to read critically.",{"children":"iv) To check your ability to read critically."}],["$","p","i) In this section you would have 12 multi-part problems total.",{"children":"i) In this section you would have 12 multi-part problems total."}],["$","p","ii) It consists of 4 problem types:- multi-source reasoning, table analysis, graphics interpretation, two- part analysis.",{"children":"ii) It consists of 4 problem types:- multi-source reasoning, table analysis, graphics interpretation, two- part analysis."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Integrated Reasoning:-",{"children":"Integrated Reasoning:-"}]]}]]}]
1b:["$","section","iii) It covers same quantitative concepts",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"iii) It covers same quantitative concepts"}],[["$","p","iv) It tests your quant and verbal skills together.",{"children":"iv) It tests your quant and verbal skills together."}],["$","p","v) Also , tests your ability to interpret and analyze graphs and tables.",{"children":"v) Also , tests your ability to interpret and analyze graphs and tables."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Analytical writing :-",{"children":"Analytical writing :-"}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","section","i) In this section you only have one problem (essay)",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"i) In this section you only have one problem (essay)"}],[["$","p","ii) You will be presented with brief argument in which you have to critique the author’s argument .",{"children":"ii) You will be presented with brief argument in which you have to critique the author’s argument ."}],["$","p","iii) It tests your logical and creative thinking.",{"children":"iii) It tests your logical and creative thinking."}],["$","p","5 EASY TIPS AND TRICKS TO CRACK (GRE) and (GMAT)",{"children":"5 EASY TIPS AND TRICKS TO CRACK (GRE) and (GMAT)"}],["$","p","1.Collect all your materials:-",{"children":"1.Collect all your materials:-"}],["$","p","Gather all your study materials you need for your exam. Books, online videos, mock papers etc. Buy some GRE and GMAT books from the market and download official GRE and GMAT apps. You can also refer to online study materials which are easily available.",{"children":"Gather all your study materials you need for your exam. Books, online videos, mock papers etc. Buy some GRE and GMAT books from the market and download official GRE and GMAT apps. You can also refer to online study materials which are easily available."}],["$","p","2.Build a strong vocabulary:-",{"children":"2.Build a strong vocabulary:-"}],["$","p","Again , the stronger the vocabulary the higher the score. Strengthening your vocabulary could help you score better in all the 3 sections of GRE. Read english books, novels, watch series,movies, listen to podcasts .",{"children":"Again , the stronger the vocabulary the higher the score. Strengthening your vocabulary could help you score better in all the 3 sections of GRE. Read english books, novels, watch series,movies, listen to podcasts ."}],["$","p","3.Take mock tests:-",{"children":"3.Take mock tests:-"}],["$","p","Practice mock tests as much as possible. It would be easy for you to understand the test format and pattern during the exam.",{"children":"Practice mock tests as much as possible. It would be easy for you to understand the test format and pattern during the exam."}],["$","p","4.Give extra time for quantitative reasoning:-",{"children":"4.Give extra time for quantitative reasoning:-"}],["$","p","In both the tests quantitative reasoning is the most important section. give special attention and time to quantitative section . In this section it requires problem solving skills, basic mathematic and arithmetic skills. Focus more on practicing and storming your brain for this section.",{"children":"In both the tests quantitative reasoning is the most important section. give special attention and time to quantitative section . In this section it requires problem solving skills, basic mathematic and arithmetic skills. Focus more on practicing and storming your brain for this section."}],["$","p","5.Manage your time:-",{"children":"5.Manage your time:-"}],["$","p","Managing your time during the test is bigger task itself. Lack of time management can make you miss out important questions and your score may drop. Practice as much as possible.",{"children":"Managing your time during the test is bigger task itself. Lack of time management can make you miss out important questions and your score may drop. Practice as much as possible."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
1d:["$","section","GMAT Exam Dates 2022:-",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"GMAT Exam Dates 2022:-"}],[["$","p","There is no proper fixed date for official GMAT exam 2022, you can choose any date according to your availability and convenience. Just in case if you need to retake the GMAT test you can do it after 16 days. You can take or retake the GMAT exam after every 16 days. Preferably , candidates are suggested to register two to three months before the actual exam date.",{"children":"There is no proper fixed date for official GMAT exam 2022, you can choose any date according to your availability and convenience. Just in case if you need to retake the GMAT test you can do it after 16 days. You can take or retake the GMAT exam after every 16 days. Preferably , candidates are suggested to register two to three months before the actual exam date."}],["$","p","If you are registering online or by phone, you can get registered as late as 24 hours before the exam date. It is safer to go for early registration as you will have a proper set schedule to prepare for the exam accordingly. Even the coaching institutes will recommend you to register at the earliest available date so that you get a plenty of time to prepare for the exam.",{"children":"If you are registering online or by phone, you can get registered as late as 24 hours before the exam date. It is safer to go for early registration as you will have a proper set schedule to prepare for the exam accordingly. Even the coaching institutes will recommend you to register at the earliest available date so that you get a plenty of time to prepare for the exam."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
